# Cloudflare Pages serves static files, so a deep link like /consumer/bills or
# a refresh on /government/agreements would 404 -- there is no file at that
# path. React Router owns those paths, so hand every unmatched request the app
# shell with a 200 (not a 301: the URL must survive for the router to read it).
# Vite copies web/public/ into dist/ verbatim, which is where Pages looks.
/*    /index.html   200
